            <ArticleTitle>Current management of hand enchondroma: a review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>191-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1142/S0218810415300028</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Enchondromas are benign bone tumours originating from cartilages. It is mainly discovered incidentally in radiographs or due to symptoms like pathological fracture or pain. Conservative treatment through regular check-up and surgical excision using curettage are the two major treatment methods for enchondromas. This review concludes that small localized asymptomatic lesions can be treated conservatively while most expanding or symptomatic lesions should be treated with simple curettage. Adjuvant treatments like high-speed burring or alcohol instillation are not recommended.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
